Subject: [PATCH] FCEA3LAB: portable, FCEA2-style interactive legacy CLI

Local changes for FCEA3LAB, an unofficial redistributable build of the NASA
CEA v3 legacy CLI (not a NASA release):

- CEA2 (FCEA2) style interactive mode: when started without arguments the
  program prompts for the case name and reads it from stdin, so
  `echo name | FCEA3LAB` and double-click use work as with FCEA2.
  (Upstream main.f90 had this as a TODO.)
- thermo.lib / trans.lib are also searched in the executable's directory and
  its data/ subdirectory (after the working directory and CEA_DATA_DIR), so the
  program works from any folder without the build-time install prefix.
  New module source/fcea3lab.F90 obtains the executable path with
  GetModuleFileNameA (Windows), _NSGetExecutablePath (macOS) or
  readlink(/proc/self/exe) (Linux/other POSIX).
- A banner identifying the build as unofficial and the database paths are
  printed on the console; the banner and thermo database path are also written
  at the top of the .out file.

Solver numerics are unchanged. Apply after 0001.

